course: dictionary
lesson: 11654
title: Artwork: pictures and designs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An artwork is something an artist has made to look at, such as a painting, drawing, sculpture or collage. Art is the big idea, and an artwork is one piece of it. «Maya hung her artwork in the school hall.» Here the artwork is one picture that can be hung on a wall.
explain: Artwork can also mean the pictures and designs in a book, magazine, game or album. «The artwork on the cover of the game was bright and full of dragons.» These pictures are not something you could hang up. They are the designs that go with the words or music.
explain: Look for clues. If the sentence is about a gallery, a school art lesson or making something, artwork means a piece of art. If it is about a cover, a game, a poster or an album, it means the pictures and designs. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: An artwork is a piece of art, such as a painting, drawing, sculpture or collage.
fact: Artwork can also mean the pictures and designs in a book, magazine, game, album or poster.
fact: «Album artwork» is the picture on the cover of a music album.
fact: «Original artwork» means the artist's own first piece, not a copy.
fact: Context clues: words like «display» or «gallery» point to a piece of art; words like «cover» or «game» point to pictures and designs.
exercise: «Maya hung her artwork in the school hall.» What is the artwork here? | The cover of a school book | A game played at lunch | A song played in the hall | *A painting or drawing that Maya made
exercise: «The artwork on the cover of the game was bright and full of dragons.» What does artwork mean here? | A piece of art hung on a wall | *The pictures and designs on the game | A story the teacher read aloud | A sculpture in the park
exercise: «Sam visited the museum to see famous artworks by painters from long ago.» Which word means more than one piece of art? | painters | museum | famous | *artworks
test: Ravi's teacher said, «Let's display your artwork on the wall tomorrow.» What does display mean here? | Sell to a shop | Hide in a box | *Show or put up for others to see | Throw away
test: «The album artwork showed a sunset over the sea.» Where would you most likely find album artwork? | On the front of a bus | Inside a sandwich bag | In a school timetable | *On the cover of a music album
exam: «The famous artist's artwork sold for a lot of money at the gallery.» Which meaning of artwork fits best? | *A piece of art, such as a painting | The pictures on a game cover | A poster for a school play | A book about how to draw
